			<div class="content" id="post-content-4856920">
									

<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> Yes</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch</strong></p>
<p>Anomalous-D (AD) is an extradimensional parasite which feeds on the pain, fear, grief or rage of other sentient entities. It became entangled with our reality and assumed human form eventually finding its way into a Foundation D Class assignment after being captured and convicted of a string of sadistic crimes against animals and people. Its position as a D Class brings it into frequent close proximity of various other anomalies. Anomalous D devises novel ways provoke or torture these anomalies undetected so that it can feed off their pain and rage.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong></p>
<p>The SCP article and addendum structure is used to tell three stories.</p>
<p>First is an incident report in which we follow a crew through routine containment maintenance when a breach occurs for unclear reasons.</p>
<p>Second, an interview log between site security of the sole surviving D-Class. The interview concludes with the sudden realization that the D-Class is anomalous. One staff is killed.</p>
<p>Third, level 4 memo looking back in retrospect and posing several questions: can other site incidents be attributed to the presence of this creature? If so, is it truly contained? Can it be used against other anomalous creatures?</p>
<p><strong>Hook / Attention Grabber:</strong></p>
<p>Following a major incident, the Foundation has confined it but is not sure that it is completely contained. Still, the possibility that this new anomaly may be used to injure or possibly destroy other anomalies is cannot be ignored.</p>
<p><strong>Additional Notes:</strong></p>
<p>Anomalous D typically resides between dimensions and might encounter various manifestations of other trans-dimensional creatures on its travels. It would not normally be able to feed on these entities as they would either be too powerful or impossible to hold on to. But in this reality it has found itself – quite accidentally – in a situation where the SCP foundation has trapped them and rendered them unable to defend themselves. Its motivation is to feed on their stress while not getting snared itself.</p>
<p>I expect that I’ll need lots of discussion and refinement to get this where I want it to be. This would be my first SCP contribution and I’m not an experienced writer. Additionally, most of what interests me in this concept are its possibilities for world-building and future story-telling. It will be challenging to bring this to life in a way that hooks the reader while also pointing to the other possibilities.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>

