															</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/digitalcat" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(7171996); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=7171996&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1609491644" alt="Digitalcat" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=7171996)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/digitalcat" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(7171996); return false;" >Digitalcat</a></span> <span class="odate time_1609398534 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">31 Dec 2020 07:08</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4858026">
									

<p>Thanks for this review. You've put a lot of work into it and I appreciate that. Having said that, I am left wondering if the content is actually this bad or if i've just failed to convey what I'm trying to do.</p>
<p>The idea came to me watching a hypercube building block demonstration. You can see it <a href="https://youtu.be/0t4aKJuKP0Q" target="_blank">here</a>.</p>
<p>I imagined how a 4+ dimensional entity would appear to us if some part of it were to intersect with our 3 D reality. I think we would perceive it as an anomaly.</p>
<p>In the story I'm trying to construct, a creature like SCP 682 is potentially vast – existing simultaneously across multiple dimensions. SCP researchers are vainly trying to terminate the thing by finding novel ways to blast the small fraction of it that they’ve snared in our reality.</p>
<p>I'm inspired to work along these lines because I'm interested in root causes. The SCP universe is now populated by something like 5000 anomalies with little sense of coherent rhyme. I'm excited by the opportunity to contribute to cannon in a way that suggests an inter-relationship between phenomena. Make some of them make a little more sense.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<blockquote>
<p>don't make this thing an interdimensional traveler.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This inter-dimensional nature of the beast is the whole point. Its existence across dimensions is what gives me the opportunity to play with interconnection between anomalies along planes that we humans don't have access to.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>don't have the Foundation recruit it as a D-Class.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>As I understand it D-Class are recruited from death row inmates. A drifter with no family who's been convicted of a sadistic murder should be at the top of their list. Additionally, from my reading, D-Class are directly exposed to anomalies all the time</p>
<blockquote>
<p>don't have there be a random breach that randomly involves the entity.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>The breach would not be random. It's triggered on purpose by the Anomalous-D while being tasked with routine maintenance. An example might be purposefully breaking eye-contact with SCP-173 while cleaning its cell in order to feed off the trauma of either the creature or the other D-Class in the room</p>
<blockquote>
<p>the Foundation has contained tons of dangerous anomalies that could injure or destroy other anomalies, but they're not clamoring to use those either</p>
</blockquote>
<p>But they have. The <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-682" target="_blank">SCP-682</a>-E addendum recounts exactly this. And it makes perfect sense. There are at least two entities that I can think of that are on a termination list and the Foundation doesn't know how they're going to kill them.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>give it more emotional/intellectual depth than &quot;does terrible things, makes people feel bad, because that's what it was conceptualized to do&quot;. Does it have any self-awareness of what has to do to survive? Does it have any redeeming qualities as an individual? This would be the main spot to flesh out, since generic danger effects are pretty common, and often seen in low-rated and deleted works.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Admittedly my thoughts here are less complete. But what I'm working with is the idea that it's a chameleon which takes on the shapes of the reality that it inhabits. It has no emotions and it's not truly sapient. It functions like an extremely sophisticated chatbot mimicking the patterns around it (I am aware of the problems of squaring that with its passing as a D-Class human for weeks).</p>
<p>It stays in one reality only as long as it can feed and then it drifts into another.</p>
<p>I'm also playing with the notion that our thoughts, souls and emotions do exist on planes that we don't have conscious access to. Yet our emotions and souls are tied to our bodies, and in that way we are all extra-dimensional beings. Anomalous-D feeds on the part of us (of all things) that's not corporal. It is able to heighten our emotional states by torturing our corporal bodies. Like squeezing juice from a fruit.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>remove the unusually insistent focus on this thing's &quot;potential&quot; usefulness.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I've highlighted its potential because I'm thinking of the stories that follow next. If this entity is to live in isolation it will be just like so many others. It will be just another mystery in a box that says nothing about the larger world and how things work together. To me that is uninteresting.</p>
</div>
</div>
